.TH WMNM 1 "September 2025" "wmnm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmnm \- NetworkManager frontend as a Window Maker dockapp
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmnm
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmnm
is a 64x64 dockapp for controlling NetworkManager, intended for Window Maker
users who want to connect to wireless networks without running nm-applet or a
full desktop environment.
.PP
The face shows the interface name, an activation LED, and, for a wifi device,
signal strength, link speed and the current network.  Clicking the interface
name at the top cycles through the devices NetworkManager knows about.
.SH USAGE
.SS Browsing networks
Scrolling over the body of the icon, or clicking it, opens the list of nearby
networks, sorted by signal strength with the active network first.  Networks
reachable through several access points appear once.
.PP
Scrolling works with the mouse wheel and with two-finger scrolling on a
touchpad.  The narrow gutter down the right of the list is a scrollbar: the
arrows at either end step by one network, and the thumb between them can be
dragged.  These matter for pointing devices with no scroll axis, such as a
touchscreen.  The arrows are dimmed when there is nothing further in that
direction.
.PP
A padlock marks a network that needs a passphrase.  A padlock with a broken
shackle marks an enterprise (802.1x) network.
.PP
The selected network's name scrolls back and forth when it is too long to fit.
.SS Connecting
Click a network to select it, then click it again to connect.  If
NetworkManager already has a matching profile it is reused and no passphrase is
asked for.
.PP
Otherwise
.B wmnm
prompts for the passphrase, hands it to NetworkManager, and NetworkManager
remembers it.  If the passphrase is rejected, the prompt reappears saying so.
.PP
Enterprise networks need an identity, an EAP method and usually a certificate,
which do not fit in a 64x64 icon, so
.B wmnm
opens
.BR nm-connection-editor (1)
instead, falling back to
.BR nmtui (1).
Once such a profile exists it activates from the list like any other.  WEP is
not supported.
.SS Captive portals
When NetworkManager reports that traffic is being intercepted,
.B wmnm
opens the portal's login page in the default browser and shows a "!" beside the
interface name.  This happens once per connection; the middle mouse button
opens it again.
.SS Keyboard
While the pointer is over the icon and the network list is open, the arrow keys
move the selection,
.B Page Up
and
.B Page Down
move by a screenful,
.B Home
and
.B End
jump to the ends,
.B Return
or
.B space
connects, and
.B Escape
returns to the device view.
.PP
A dockapp never receives the keyboard focus, so
.B wmnm
grabs the keyboard in order to see these keys at all.  The grab is taken only
while the network list is open and the pointer is inside the icon, and is
dropped as soon as the pointer leaves, so it cannot interfere with typing
elsewhere.
.SH MOUSE BUTTONS
.TP
.B Button 1
Cycle devices (on the interface name), select or connect (in the network list).
.TP
.B Button 2
Reopen the captive portal login page.
.TP
.B Button 3
Return to the device view.
.TP
.B Buttons 4 and 5
Scroll the network list.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-windowed
Run in a normal window instead of as a dockapp.  Useful for testing outside
Window Maker.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WMNM_ASKPASS
Program to use for passphrase prompts, overriding the search described in
.BR wmnm-askpass (1).
.SH NOTES
NetworkManager asks registered secret agents for passphrases in sequence and
takes the first answer.  If nm-applet, gnome-shell or plasma-nm is also
running, its dialog may appear instead of
.BR wmnm-askpass (1).
Run only one of them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmnm-askpass (1),
.BR nmcli (1),
.BR nm-connection-editor (1),
.BR nmtui (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Doug Torrance <dtorrance@piedmont.edu>
